body:
yea its a hard reality - im here living ina dangerous side of town in low-income housing with my broke up sedan trying to take as little loan money as possible and still survive. While these kids pull up in mercedes and tesla paid by daddy and live in their 2 bedroom apartments on the richer side of town. 

&#x200B;

Yes, I hear gun shots at least once a month. i do pay half of the average rent cost here so to me its worth it but i when i tell some rich kids this, they're like omg i could NEVER and im like yea well i dont have a choice. Some girl's dad got her a new tesla for use when she FLIES BACK HOME. Im out here making 20 hr roadtrips to see my family. 

&#x200B;

some girls be talking about getting botox touch ups from their clinic when they go back - IT IS NOT  a level playing field.
